  - animal welfare
  - legislation
abstract: >
  A structured, provision-level dataset coding penalty structure, scope of
  application, enforcement mechanism, and linked policy-effect evidence for
  animal anti-cruelty / animal protection law across 23 jurisdictions
  (Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Macau, Japan, South Korea, Singapore,
  United States federal, Canada federal, England and Wales, Scotland,
  Northern Ireland, the European Union, Germany, France, Switzerland,
  the Netherlands, Italy, Spain, Australia federal, New South Wales,
  Victoria, and New Zealand). Applies a policy-surveillance / legal-
  epidemiology coding methodology, not previously applied to this legal
  domain, with an explicit three-tier source-verification scheme
  (verified / snippet / unverified) shipped alongside the data. THIS IS A
  DRAFT RELEASE: an independent human verification pass over the coded
  content is in progress and not yet complete. The verification_tier field
  describes source retrieval quality, not human review status.
